1. Verify the exact subject paths, file hashes, symlink target strings, map program identity, and map intrinsic identity above. If a material coordinate differs, return invalid_basis and identify the mismatch before evaluating purpose fit.

2. Start from the logical constraint map. Inspect only the linked symbols, clauses, residuals, and source routes material to this review. Do not load the entire Source STDO corpus by default.

3. Compare the exact eight-member candidate with the stated-purpose authority. Test whether the candidate actually preserves:
- LLM ownership of semantic interpretation, frame selection, labels, text, ordering, diagnostics consumption, and revision;
- exact Axiom Indexer ownership of only URI resolution, mechanical validation, logical-map instantiation, and pure joining;
- map-first pickup, visible frame URI/purpose/source route, and bounded exact-source re-entry;
- source-linked symbols, operative clauses, explicit uncertainty, and honest structural-versus-semantic limits;
- one canonical skill with target-specific references that alter presentation only;
- exact eight-member thin Product shape and correct relative discovery symlinks;
- Worker/Reviewer/Executive boundaries as instructions rather than a claimed deterministic packet engine; and
- exclusion of full M_b, GTL, GraphFunctions, ABG runtime, hidden orchestration, automatic frame selection, semantic acceptance, provider-attestation gates, and release inference.

4. Independently seek falsifiers. At minimum test for: hidden automatic context selection; source routes that cannot recover a material claim; a materially wrong or omitted governing constraint; false confidence from validation; target-reference semantic drift; broken discovery indirection; candidate/map identity mismatch; Product-member leakage; role drift; and any claim that a working map is accepted Source STDO, a full M_b, GTL, or a released Product.

5. Re-enter exact source only when the map, a residual, disagreement, or unresolved meaning requires it. For semantic comparison, use a bounded adversarial sample spanning at least: a_c layer and structural/semantic separation; specification authority flow; reference-frame and role boundaries; release exactness; compression/source re-entry; and template/schema structural limits. Record every source URI opened, why it was needed, what constraint it recovered or challenged, and whether the loading was necessary.

6. You may run non-mutating inspection and the exact installed validator in stdout-only mode. Do not write reports, regenerated maps, temporary candidate files, caches, or fixes. Treat existing tests and dogfood reports as claims to inspect, not substitutes for source comparison.

7. Assess purpose fit, not general repository cleanliness and not the deferred three-level/GTL direction. Adjacent observations belong in a short separate section only when they materially affect the stated thin-candidate claim.
